# Resilix Code Generation Rules (for Cursor Ask / AI)

## Function Format
- Export as: `export function name(args): ReturnType`
- Pure functions only: input → output, no side effects
- Max 25 lines per function (excluding comments)
- JSDoc required for public exports

## Testing
- Every new function needs `tests/[name].test.js`
- Tests must cover: happy path, edge case, invalid input
- Run: `node tests/[name].test.js` — must exit 0 on pass
- No external test libs (use Node.js assert only)

## Validation
- All JSON output must match `data/schema.json`
- Run `scripts/validate_json.py <file>` before commit
- CI fails on schema mismatch or lint error

## File Structure
- New logic → `src/[feature].js`
- New tests → `tests/[feature].test.js`
- New data → `data/demo/[client].json`
- No changes to `docs/index.html` without ISSUE link

## Output Constraints
- Bundle size: <10KB minified per module
- No external dependencies (vanilla JS / Python stdlib)
- Must work offline (GitHub Pages)
- EN strings only in code; RU via i18n map

## Commit Rules
- One ISSUE per commit: `feat: [ISSUE#N] short desc`
- Include validation step in commit message
- Run `git diff --stat` before push

## AI Editing Rules
- Use atomic shell commands only
- Never output long markdown/code blocks
- For file edits: use `python3 << 'PY' ... PY` or base64
- After each edit: show `git diff --stat` summary
